config ZMK_BATTERY_REPORT
    bool "Publish battery levels as custom settings"
    depends on ZMK_BATTERY_REPORTING
    select ZMK_CUSTOM_SETTINGS
    help
      Publishes each half's battery percentage where Keeb-On! Studio can read
      it. ZMK reports a battery level over the BLE Battery Service, which is
      only visible to a host that is connected over Bluetooth -- the app sees
      nothing over USB, which is exactly where someone diagnosing a keyboard
      that will not stay connected tends to be.

      The levels travel as ordinary custom settings, written in temporary
      mode: they never reach flash and never count as an unsaved change.

if ZMK_BATTERY_REPORT

config ZMK_BATTERY_REPORT_STUDIO_RPC
    bool "Expose the battery levels to Studio"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO
    select ZMK_CUSTOM_SETTINGS_STUDIO_RPC
    help
      Registers this module as a Studio custom subsystem. There is no RPC of
      its own, but a setting whose subsystem id matches no registered
      subsystem is dropped from ListSettings, so without this the levels
      exist on the keyboard and the app cannot see them.

module = ZMK_BATTERY_REPORT
module-str = zmk_battery_report
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ZMK_BATTERY_REPORT
